# Every hour, take a backup if the newest one is BACKUP_EVERY_DAYS (7)
# days old or more. Checking hourly rather than firing once a week means
# a week whose planned time the Mac slept through still gets its backup,
# within the hour of the Mac being back. Output goes to the container's
# log: docker logs kma_auth_backup.
17 * * * * sh /backup.sh due > /proc/1/fd/1 2>&1
